# Lead Scout — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values.
# NEVER commit .env or .env.local to source control.
# These variables are read server-side only (Vercel serverless functions).
# They are NEVER exposed to the browser or included in the client bundle.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required: Google Places API key
#
# How to obtain:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   2. Create (or select) a project
#   3. Enable these APIs:
#      - Places API (or Places API (New))
#      - Geocoding API
#   4. Create an API key under "Credentials"
#   5. Restrict the key to the above two APIs (recommended)
#   6. For production: add HTTP referrer restrictions to your domain
#
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT: Do NOT use a VITE_ prefix here.
#     VITE_* variables are injected into the client bundle by Vite
#     and will be visible in the browser — that would expose your key.
#     This variable is only available inside /api/* serverless functions.
#
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
